    <string name="gn_label">Guide number</string>
    <string name="gn_support">At ISO 100, full power. Lower it for bounce.</string>
    <string name="gn_error">Use %1$s–%2$s</string>
    <string name="formula_title">The calculation</string>
    <string name="formula_body">f-number = guide number ÷ distance in meters. Guide number = base GN × √(ISO ÷ 100) × √(power). Full power is 1, 1/2 is 0.5, 1/4 is 0.25, and so on.</string>
    <string name="chart_title">Distance chart</string>
    <string name="chart_caption">Meters at ISO %1$d and GN %2$s. Tap a row to use that power. The iM30 manual prints the same table, rounded to one decimal.</string>
    <string name="chart_power">Power</string>
    <string name="limits_title">Where it drifts</string>
    <string name="limits_body">Hold the phone at the flash, not at arm\'s length from another spot. The published guide number assumes direct flash and an average subject. Blank walls and dim rooms make the distance less sure. The FM sync speed does not change with the lens.</string>
